                <pb facs="1132" n="846" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg846"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72115/2679</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Elkus</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-21T09:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 21, 1916, 9 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 26, 8.30 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2349. My 2333, December 14, 10 p. m. The Sublime Porte informs Embassy that the
                    arrests of Russians are due to capture of Moslems at Terma on the Black Sea
                    coast near Samsun by the Russian Fleet. The Sublime Porte further states that it
                    has demanded release of these Moslems within 8 days from December 17 through the
                    Spanish Legation, and that unless they are released the arrested Russians will
                    be exiled to interior. Of those arrested up to 19th, all excepting 22 have been
                    released through my personal efforts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Elkus</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
